# shellcheck shell=bash

# Name advertised to iPhone, iPad, and macOS clients. Leave it unset to get a
# host-qualified default like "Kast Receiver (hostname)", so two kast boxes on
# the same LAN don't show up as identical entries. Uncomment to pin a fixed name.
#UXPLAY_NAME="Kast Receiver"

# Extra arguments forwarded to uxplay.
# Ships with -pin so a sender must enter a PIN before it can mirror — the
# receiver listens on the whole LAN, so this gates access. With bare -pin, uxplay
# shows a fresh random 4-digit PIN on the receiving screen for each connection;
# use "-pin 2468" for a fixed code. Remove -pin entirely for open receiving.
# Other examples: UXPLAY_ARGS=(-h265 -pin)
UXPLAY_ARGS=(-pin)

# Name advertised by the AirPlay AUDIO receiver (shairport-sync), separate from
# the screen-mirroring receiver above. Host-qualified default like the screen
# receiver; uncomment to pin a fixed name.
#SHAIRPORT_NAME="Kast Audio"

# Extra arguments forwarded to shairport-sync, e.g. SHAIRPORT_ARGS=(-v).
SHAIRPORT_ARGS=()

# Name advertised by the YouTube DIAL receiver. Host-qualified default;
# uncomment to pin a fixed name.
#YT_RECEIVER_NAME="Kast YouTube"

# With autoplay off (default), deliberately casting a video still plays it, but a
# device that merely connects to the DIAL receiver can't start playback on its
# own (DIAL has no pairing, so that would be any device on the LAN). Set to 1 to
# restore connect-autoplay on a trusted network.
#KAST_YT_AUTOPLAY=1

# Make "Display Cast…" drop Wi-Fi by default (1) or keep it (0). Needed for
# Miracast on single-radio adapters. Editable from Kast preferences.
KAST_DROP_WIFI_DEFAULT=0
